    "sourceSha256": "87318f22057e91f9eb22ba6610d16753f3dae2d2da07ef0689f8048a716d2e98",
    "sourceWikitext": "__NOTOC__{{recipe summary\n| category = Bread recipes\n| servings = 4\n| time = \n| difficulty = 3\n| image = [[File:10 Steamed Bread - Congee Village House.jpg|300px]]\n| energy = \n| note = \n}}\n{{Recipe}}\n\n'''Alkubus''' is a steamed wheat bread from northern Nigeria.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Alkubus {{!}} Traditional Bread From Nigeria {{!}} TasteAtlas |url=https://www.tasteatlas.com/alkubus |access-date=2023-12-26 |website=www.tasteatlas.com}}</ref> It originated from Arabs.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n*2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Wheat Flour|wheat flour]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] instant [[Cookbook:Yeast|yeast]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n*½ cup water\n*2 teaspoons [[Cookbook:Peanut Oil|vegetable oil]]\n\n== Special equipment ==\n*Mold for cooking\n*[[Cookbook:Steaming|Steamer]]\n*[[Cookbook:Cooktop|Stovetop]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# [[Cookbook:Sifting|Sift]] the flour into a mixing bowl. Mix in the yeast, salt, and baking powder. \n# Mix in the water to make a [[Cookbook:Dough|dough]], and knead it until cohesive and fully combined.\n# Cover the dough and let rise for 1 hour.\n# Gently deflate the dough.\n# Grease a cooking mold, and transfer the dough to the mold.\n# Cover the mold and place it in a steamer setup. [[Cookbook:Steaming|Steam]] until cooked through and a [[Cookbook:Skewer|skewer]] inserted into the center comes out clean.\n# Remove from the heat and let cool.\n# Unmold the steamed bread and serve.\n\n== References ==\n[[category:Inexpensive recipes]]\n[[Category:Hausa recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n<references />\n[[Category:Steamed recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using yeast]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes for bread]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]",
